{
  "description": "Resource files as the build step writes them, each with the embedded bundle's manifest as a reader reads it: the project's configuration with the channel resolved to its id, the SDK options and their defaults, the build-time facts, and the files and updates hosts in a build against staging or the local stack alone. The embedded bundle's manifest is the bundle manifest, the same whether the build step registered the bundle or not; embeddedBundleId is null when it did not. embeddedBundleManifest is null in a build that bundled no JavaScript, a React Native or Expo debug build: its build step registers no binary and asks the API nothing, so embeddedBundleId is null with it, and the SDK answers skipped with build_debug. channelId is null in a build whose build step ran without a token or offline and could not resolve the channel's name; that build registers nothing either. publicKeys are the project's public keys as the build step re-encoded them for the platform the file is written for, so the platform's own API imports them with no ASN.1 handled on the device: each { der, keyId }, der the base64 of the PKCS #1 DER on iOS and of the SPKI DER on Android, keyId the key id: `sha256:` and the hex SHA-256 of the SPKI bytes, which a signature names. refusedResourceFiles are files a reader refuses, each an accepted file with one fault, so each pins one rule: a checkIntervalSeconds below 60, the floor, since a zero made the core check in a tight loop; an applyStrategy outside the catalog; a value of the wrong type; a null where a key may be absent but not null; a missing fingerprint, embeddedBundleId, channelId or embeddedBundleManifest; an empty fingerprint, channelId or keyId; an embeddedBundleId outside the identifier charset; a host that is not a URL; a public key without its keyId or in the self-describing form; and a der that is not canonical base64.",
